! REPRODUCER, an ASSEMBLER finding already on the list as G3.1
! (docs/source_audit.md, "G3 -- Assembler completeness"), cut here
! because C22-6578 Chapter 4 prints it three times and says so itself.
! strap_asm.py refused this deck until 2026-11-16:
!
!   cannot parse expression 'N*N-1.0' at '*N-1.0'
!
! It now assembles it as STRAP II does (G3.1, strap_asm._arith_bi), to the
! word below; tests/check_field_arithmetic.py holds the arithmetic.
!
! The statement is C22-6578 printed p.42, Problem 4.8 (product of
! square matrices): "V-ICR,$3,N*N-1.0".  The page's comment (a):
! "STRAP I does not perform multiplication of addresses, but STRAP II
! will do it properly."  Printed p.40, Problem 4.6 Method 3, has
! "SF(BU,N*N,N), LOC" with the same remark: "The store field
! instruction will not be assembled correctly by STRAP I, because of
! the multiplication in the data description field.  STRAP II will do
! it properly."
!
! WHAT IT ASSEMBLES TO is NOT 63.0, as this header used to say.  N is an
! integer (N SYN, 8), and an integer in a 19-bit field counts HALF words
! (C28-6129 Section I printed pp.8-9, "INTEGER ADDRESSES"): N*N is 64
! half words, less the bit address 1.0, two half words: 62 half words,
! 31.0.  The host STRAP II assembles exactly that (0007C70F, where
! "V-ICR,$3,63.0" is 000FC70F), and so does 4.8's printed program, which
! is wrong for that reason (decks/problem_4_8.strap; docs/NEXT.md
! "PROBLEMS 4.6-4.8").  The control below, 63.0, is only a card that
! assembles.
! tests/check_problem_4_dd_refusals.py asserted the refusal; it now asserts
! the word, 0007C70F 00083000, under strap_asm.

N       SYN, 8
START   V-ICR,$3,N*N-1.0
        BEW, $
        END, START
